S("BfRyPzy-e-k","Make Lush & Dubby Synths (Like Traumer, Kolter & Janaret)",
 "dub-stab-family-detuned-saw-lp24-res-hp120-drawn-cutoff-dual-bandpass-lfo-sidechained-dub-verb",
 "Dub-techno/house stab family: two detuned saws (osc 2 nudged toward square) into a resonant 24 dB low-pass at ~100 Hz with envelope amount ~48 and a 120 Hz high-pass, soft attack, hand-drawn cutoff automation that differs each repeat, dual resonant band-pass filters swept by a 1-2 bar LFO plus chorus, a long 'dub verb' return sidechained to the kick, a longer (6 s) verb and echoes automated up in breakdowns, all built on one four-note minor chord (root triad plus the note 2 semitones below the root)",
 "Build 3-5 call-and-response chord stabs that sound like one source and keep moving without any pitch randomness. Delta vs filter/phaser clusters: a full stab-family recipe in which the movement comes from drawn cutoff automation and dual band-pass sweeps rather than LFO-on-cutoff, with kick-sidechained reverb returns that pump with the groove and breakdown-only reverb-length automation.",
 ["A two-oscillator synth with a resonant LP and an HP filter and a mod matrix (any wavetable/VA synth)","A dual-filter or phaser effect, chorus, 2 long reverbs, delay/echo, sidechain compressor, glue compressor, saturator"],
 [("key","string","e.g. A minor",True),("kick","audio","Kick for sidechaining the reverb return",True)],
 [("stab_group","audio/midi","Grouped stab layers sharing returns, with breakdown automation")],
 ["Pitch stays fixed: movement is drawn filter automation and filter/LFO sweeps only, with no random pitch or note variation (Matt's preference).","Use at most two chord types per track (e.g. Am add the note a tone below the root, plus Em).","Echo throws are sparse: no rapid repeats or clicking rolls.","Drums (kick) enter early (~8 counts / ~12 s) so the sidechained verb has something to pump against."],
 [("Osc 1 saw, osc 2 saw with its wave position nudged toward square, and detune osc 2.","Synth oscillators","Lush detuned base tone"),
  ("Filter 1: low-pass 24 dB, clean, high resonance, cutoff ~100 Hz. Filter 2: high-pass ~120 Hz to clear lows.","Synth filters","Dark resonant stab with no mud"),
  ("Amp envelope with a slightly softened attack; route an envelope to filter 1 cutoff (amount ~48). Use a longer decay for the main downbeat stab and shorter ones for answers.","Envelopes + mod matrix","Warm, non-harsh stab that opens and closes"),
  ("Draw cutoff automation by hand (or record a knob) and make each repeat's shape slightly different, instead of an LFO on cutoff.","Automation lane","Natural, evolving movement with pitch unchanged"),
  ("Insert a dual filter: two resonant band-pass filters with quite a lot of resonance (the auto-captions give the setting only as 'four'; set by ear), swept by a 1-2 bar LFO at ~50% depth; then a chorus. A phaser is a weaker substitute.","Dual filter + chorus","Phasey, dubby character"),
  ("Chord: minor triad plus the note two semitones below the root (A minor: A C E + G below), optionally plus the 7th (B). Answer stabs reuse it with shorter notes, snappier envelopes and one osc.","MIDI","Cohesive call-and-response family"),
  ("Send all stabs to a 'dub verb' return (long, ~4 s, lush) sidechained to the kick; add echo; add a second, longer (~6 s) reverb whose send/decay rises in breakdowns; keep a third echo mainly for breakdowns.","Returns + sidechain","Reverb pumps with the groove and swells in breakdowns"),
  ("Group the stabs: saturator for edge, insert reverb to glue, low-shelf cut on low mids, glue compressor at ~25% wet, and an auto filter that slopes down in the breakdown and reopens; finish with gentle tube warmth.","Group chain","Stabs sound like one source; breakdown gets deeper then opens")],
 ["Only filter/FX parameters move; note pitches are fixed with no random modulation.","Reverb return gain-reduction meter moves with each kick hit.","No more than two chord types are used; the main chord contains the note a whole tone below the root."],
 ["dub-techno","stab","chord-stab","filter-automation","band-pass","dual-filter","phaser","reverb-send","sidechain","breakdown"])

S("HyXvY_PXI9Q","How to Turn Samples into Synths",
 "sample-to-synth-keygroup-mono-lowpass-env-pluck-resonance-square-lfo-steps-octave-layer-through-one-filter-reversed-octave-granular",
 "Turn a static one-shot or multisample into a playable synth with subtractive tools: map it chromatically, mono or poly with a set release, a low-pass with envelope depth for sweeps or plucks, resonance for acid, an eighth-note square LFO for stepped filter jumps, layer an octave copy (or different samples) through one filter so they fuse, then distortion/chorus, a reversed octave-up granular layer and reverb",
 "Hybrid synthesis on any sampler or groovebox that has filters and FX but no synth engine. Delta vs granular cluster (sampler loop chord pad) and filter cluster: a sample-as-oscillator subtractive patch recipe, where layered samples share one filter to become a single, unrecognisable instrument.",
 ["A sampler with keygroup/multisample mapping, filter + envelope, LFO and insert FX (DAW sampler, MPC, Digitakt etc.)","One or more pitched synth samples (e.g. bass and a higher pad/lead)"],
 [("samples","audio","Pitched one-shots or multisamples, root note known",True)],
 [("sampled_synth","instrument","Playable patch with filter sweep/pluck, stepped LFO and layered FX")],
 ["Portamento, vibrato and fast auto-pan from the video are left out or kept minimal: no wobbly or random pitch (Matt's preference).","Chorus/ensemble can cause phase issues, so check mono.","The LFO is tempo-synced (e.g. 1/8) and steady, not random."],
 [("Load the sample as a keygroup/chromatic program with the root set correctly; for bass choose one-shot + mono, for chords choose poly with a longer amp release.","Sampler","Sample playable across the keyboard"),
  ("Engage a low-pass filter, turn the cutoff down and the envelope depth up: a slower decay gives a sweep, a short decay gives a pluck.","Filter + envelope","Static sample becomes a pluck or sweep"),
  ("Raise resonance for an acid character, or raise amp attack and hold for a swelling pad.","Filter resonance / amp env","Distinct voices from one sample"),
  ("Assign a square LFO synced to 1/8 to cutoff with moderate depth for rhythmic stepped filter jumps.","LFO","Tempo-locked filter steps"),
  ("Layer a second copy of the sample an octave up (or a different sample), adjust pan and level, and run both through the same filter.","Sample layers","Layers fuse into one new instrument"),
  ("Add FX to taste: gentle distortion to thicken, chorus (check phase), a granular layer pitched +12 and reversed for space, and reverb.","Insert FX","Unrecognisable, cinematic result"),
  ("Optionally resample the result or use the sample as a wavetable/granular source in a synth for further shaping.","Resample / wavetable","Reusable sound for future tracks")],
 ["The program plays in tune across at least two octaves from the root.","Filter envelope depth is non-zero and audibly sweeps or plucks.","Layered copies share one filter (one cutoff control moves both)."],
 ["hybrid-synthesis","sampler","subtractive","filter-envelope","lfo","layering","granular","resampling"])
